2802       data a (drop=i);
2803       do i=1 to 1000;
2804       x1=rannor(1234);
2805       x2=rannor(1234);
2806       e=rannor(1234);
2807       if i > 950 then y=100 + 10*e;
2808       else y=10 + 5*x1 + 3*x2 + 0.5 * e;
2809       output;
2810       end;
2811       run;

NOTE: The data set WORK.A has 1000 observations and 4 variables.

2812       proc quantreg data=a;
2813       model y = x1 x2 / seed=314159;
2814       run;

NOTE: No valid quantiles are specified. PROC QUANTREG computes median regression.
NOTE: The PROCEDURE QUANTREG printed page 180.

2815       proc quantreg algorithm=interior(tolerance=1e-6)
2816       ci=none data=a;
2817       model y = x1 x2 / itprint nosummary seed=314159;
2818       run;

NOTE: No valid quantiles are specified. PROC QUANTREG computes median regression.
